<question type="description"><name><text>Module 1 · Lesson 0 · Section 5: The Story — Part 0</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<h3>Section 5: The Story — Part 0</h3>
<p><strong>The Scribe’s Beginning</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> The story in this introductory lesson (‘The
Scribe’s Beginning’) is a standalone narrative used to practice the
alphabet. The main course narrative (The Acts of Mar Yukhannan) begins
in Lesson 1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>Narrative note: Before the Acts of Mar Yukhannan begin, we see
the scribe, Addai, preparing the parchment. This part introduces the
visual rhythm of the script.</em></p>
<div class="sentence">
<p><span class="sentence-syriac">ܐܢܐ ܥܕܝ ܣܦܪܐ</span> <span
class="sentence-translit">ʾenā ʿAdday sāp̄rā.</span> <span
class="sentence-gloss">ʾenā (I) ʿAdday (Addai) sāp̄rā (the-scribe)</span>
<span class="sentence-translation">I am Addai the scribe.</span></p>
</div>
<div class="sentence">
<p><span class="sentence-syriac">ܟܬܒ ܐܢܐ ܡܠܬܐ ܕܐܠܗܐ</span> <span
class="sentence-translit">kāteb ʾenā meltā d-Alāhā.</span> <span
class="sentence-gloss">kāteb (writing) ʾenā (I) meltā (the-word) d- (of)
Alāhā (God)</span> <span class="sentence-translation">I am writing the
word of God.</span></p>
</div>
<div class="sentence">
<p><span class="sentence-syriac">ܗܢܘ ܟܬܒܐ ܕܝܘܚܢܢ</span> <span
class="sentence-translit">hannū ktābā d-Yūḥannan.</span> <span
class="sentence-gloss">hannū (this-is) ktābā (the-writing/book) d- (of)
Yūḥannan (John)</span> <span class="sentence-translation">This is the
book of Yukhannan.</span></p>
</div>
<hr />

]]></text></questiontext></question>
